            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates repair heavy commercial parking lot damage in Westborough, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates inspects sub-base stability using heavy test-rolling equipment. Severely deteriorated pavement is milled down 2 to 3 inches using commercial milling machines. Crews repair damaged aggregate sub-bases with compacted gravel, apply a liquid tack coat binder, and pave a 2-inch dense hot-mix asphalt top course sealed with commercial traffic line striping.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What site preparation is required before installing a concrete paver patio in Westborough, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates excavates native soil 8 to 10 inches deep, installs geotextile stabilization fabric, and compacts a 6-inch processed gravel base using vibratory plate compactors. Pavers are set on a 1-inch bed of washed concrete sand and joint-sealed with polymeric sand to prevent weed growth and frost shifting in Westborough.</p>
